AYRE ANALYSIS

An interesting evolution is storing patterns rather than projects.

Example:

Patterns/
├── LockOnPattern
├── InventoryPattern
├── DialoguePattern
├── QuestPattern
├── ArenaPattern
└── SaveSystemPattern

Then a new game becomes:

Game
=
Selected Patterns
+
Configuration

Over years of development, you would accumulate a personal game-development corpus.

The result is less:

Build Game

and more:

Assemble Proven Systems

At that point Unity AI is not inventing solutions.

It is reconstructing implementations from a growing library of validated knowledge, decisions, and patterns that Raven has accumulated across projects.
